  "description": "Fuaran.Core.CSharp (Phase 128) — a C#-shaped facade over the closed F# unions a non-F# authoring veneer has to construct and read: the column layer (CellValue, TableValue, SourceValue and the column vocabularies), the artifact-function hole-declaration family (ValueSpace / HoleKind / HoleDecl / EffectClass / Signature), and the wire JSON model (JVal). Construction is factory methods, reading is Match / Switch, and nothing but the declared ToCore / FromCore bridge mentions an F# option, list, function or union type — so a C# or VB veneer can keep a strict \"every authored value passes through the declared surface\" rule instead of reflecting into F# union cases or hand-rolling a mirror. .NET-only: this package is NOT part of the Fable-clean set (a C# assembly is not Fable-compiled), and it adds no surface to the F# packages it wraps.",
